      "description": "Philosophy programs covering ethics, logic, metaphysics, political philosophy, and the history of ideas, including great-books and philosophy-politics-economics style pathways.",
      "tips": [
        {
          "kind": "extracurricular",
          "title": "Join a debate club or Ethics Bowl team",
          "detail": "Structured argument is the core skill philosophy programs build on. Debate, model parliament, and Ethics Bowl give you regular practice constructing and defending positions, and concrete results to cite in supplementary applications.",
          "sortOrder": 0
        },
        {
          "kind": "extracurricular",
          "title": "Read widely and keep a written record",
          "detail": "Work through serious books beyond the curriculum and write as you go — essays, reviews, or a blog. A visible body of writing is the clearest evidence of sustained interest in ideas that an arts application can show.",
          "sortOrder": 1
        },
        {
          "kind": "extracurricular",
          "title": "Write math or logic contests",
          "detail": "Formal logic sits at the centre of a philosophy degree. Contests such as the CSMC or Euclid signal the rigorous, step-by-step reasoning philosophy departments value, even though the contest content is mathematical.",
          "sortOrder": 2
        }
      ]
    }
